# Addresses whose lane offsets or trip shifts pass 2^63 bytes: summed in
# i64 they overflowed and a debug build panicked. A lane or loop part
# past 2^62 bytes is now left uncounted: the warp's sectors are unknown,
# and the loop's unique bytes, though ptxas stores 4 B on each of 8
# distinct addresses.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/offsets_wide.ptx | FileCheck "%s"
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_offsets_wide_lanes
CHECK: st.global.u32  global store 4 B  warp: ? (lane offsets reach 2^62 bytes)  [18014398509481984 * %tid.x + param_0]
CHECK-LABEL: kernel micro_offsets_wide_trips
CHECK: trips = 8
CHECK: global bytes per CTA over the loop's own blocks: requested 32 B, unique unknown
